# Filter Hz 1.3.0: DELAY HPF and LPF locked on trig 1 (GRID RECORDING) show hertz in wide
# boxes, and LPF follows the trig's HPF lock, not the track's HPF.
# Track HPF 38, LPF 40; trig 1 held, each knob nudged twice (the first nudge locks the shown
# value, the second moves it): locks HPF 39, LPF 41. Expected 79.0Hz and 1.44kHz (39 + 41).
# Then track HPF set to 0, trig 1 held again (a re-hold shows no values) and LPF nudged once
# more to 42: expected 1.55kHz (the trig's HPF 39 + 42), not 97.7Hz (the track's HPF 0 + 42).
# Ends by tapping T1 in GRID RECORDING, which takes the lock trig and its locks off, and puts
# HPF 38, LPF 40 back. Needs step 1 of the FX track's pattern empty at the start.
name: filter-hz-delay-lock
state: changes
# FX is a toggle (pressed on the FX track it goes back to the drum track), so BD is selected first.
hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key FX
key SRC
wait 3500
cc 20 38
cc 21 40
key RECORD
hold T1
nudge E +1
nudge E +1
nudge F +1
nudge F +1
wait 750
screen locked
expect locked == ref region 0 40 128 15
release T1
cc 20 0
wait 300
hold T1
nudge F +1
wait 750
screen again
expect again == ref region 0 40 128 15
release T1
wait 300
key T1
wait 300
key RECORD
cc 20 38
cc 21 40
